+# A caption-split alias still matches, within one cue — Plan
+
+Implements **OD-6** (`docs/DESIGN.oracle.md`), which adds **R1002** from the
+evidence in **BL-8**, together with **OD-15**, which adds **R1010** from the
+evidence in **BL-16** and fixes the text R1002's rule runs over. Measured
+offline against the shipped table, `toma hawk`, `aor us master` and
+`air us elite` matched nothing at all — three boards invisible in the corpus
+every later stage is built from. OD-15 then scoped the rule to one cue's text
+and required the scoped-out case to be counted rather than lost.
+
+This plan is re-cut from the draft preserved at `docs/oracle/od-6-plan-draft.md`
+(closed PR #85), used as raw material and not as authority, per that file's own
+header and the 2026-08-20 run-2 handoff.
+
+## Summary
+
+Three mechanical changes to the space the matcher works in, a counter for the
+case the rule deliberately does not reach, and BL-8's variant set as a fixture.
+
+- **The hyphen stops being a kept character.** `normalize` folds it to a space,
+  so `steel-legend` meets the table's `steel legend`. Two shipped `normalize`
+  tests assert the retired rule and are rewritten. Only hyphens fold.
+- **Each surface form compiles to a split-tolerant pattern** — an optional space
+  between adjacent characters inside a word, a *required* space where the form
+  itself has one. `tomahawk` matches `toma hawk`, `aorus master` matches
+  `aor us master`. Still one pattern, longest form first, so R22 and R23 hold.
+- **A fused token is never matched into.** `b650` is not found in `theb650` and
+  `aorus master` does not match `aorusmaster`. Pinned as negative cases.
+- **The rule runs over one cue at a time (R1010).** `find_mentions` keeps its
+  shape and its `start_seconds`. A split across a cue boundary yields **no**
+  mention — and is counted: `select`'s report gains a per-run line, zero
+  included, for matches that exist only in the join of two adjacent cues.
+- **That counter costs the owner one thing:** `data/selected.jsonl` gains a key
+  (`Selection` and `ThresholdReport` each gain an integer), and a file written
+  before this plan is refused with "re-run `select`" rather than read as zero.
+- **The table gains `airus elite` and `airus master`, and loses `pro-rs`** —
+  `air us` for `aorus` is a mishearing no join recovers, and `pro-rs` folds onto
+  the `pro rs` beside it once slice 1 lands.
+- **The 52-variant set is reconstructed, not recovered.** BL-8's list was never
+  committed; the fixture rebuilds 52 from the shipped table by BL-8's own damage
+  classes, its three failures verbatim, and says in the file that it is one.
+- **Not done here:** OD-7/R1003's ITX rule, cross-cue *matching* (counted only,
+  per OD-15), OD-11/R1007's move of the table, separators beyond the hyphen.
+
+Four slices, ~710 lines, **sequential**; no new dependency, no gate change, and
+nothing here touches the network. Three uncertainties, all LOW, all proceeded
+on; one is filed as **BL-17**.
+
+**What I need you to rule on:**
+
+1. **The reconstructed 52.** R1002 asks for BL-8's set by that number and the
+   set is not in the repository. If a fixture of the observed failures alone is
+   honester, slice 4 shrinks to those.
+2. **The counter's arithmetic at a fused boundary** — filed as BL-17, built on
+   the default below. It moves a diagnostic, nothing that gates.
+3. **Merge order.** OD-7 (R1003) edits the same matcher and OD-11 (R1007) moves
+   the same table file; whichever lands second carries the rebase.
+
+## Uncertainties
+
+Three, all **LOW**, all proceeded on and recorded here. One (the counter's
+arithmetic) is new to this plan and is filed as **BL-17** under "Uncertainties
+awaiting oracle ruling" in `docs/BACKLOG.md`, in this same commit. Two are
+restated from the preserved draft: the 2026-08-20 run-2 handoff records that
+this oracle read both defaults and found them sound, and directed that they
+travel in the plan without `BL-<n>` ids — so they are reviewed, not silent, and
+filing them again would ask for a ruling that was already given.
+
+- **Q:** What exactly does the cross-cue counter count when the join *changes*
+  an existing match rather than creating one? R1010 describes the case two ways
+  — "matches that exist only in the normalized concatenation of adjacent cues"
+  and "a match that starts in one cue's text and ends in the next's" — which
+  agree everywhere except one shape: a cue ending `...b650` followed by one
+  beginning `e board`, where the join normalizes to `b650e board` and turns one
+  B650 mention into one B650E mention. The first reading counts 0 (no mention
+  was lost), the second counts 1. Offsets cannot arbitrate: normalization fuses
+  the boundary, so there is no boundary position left in the joined text to test
+  a span against. — **risk:** LOW — the signature is `-> int` either way, the
+  slice boundary is the same, the number is a diagnostic that gates nothing, and
+  reversing it is an edit inside one function. — **proposed:** the first
+  reading, as **mentions lost**: per adjacent pair, matches in the joined
+  normalized text minus matches in each cue's own normalized text, floored at
+  zero. It is computable, it is what "what this ruling scoped out" means, and it
+  makes a nonzero count directly comparable with the mentions that were emitted.
+  **Ruling:** proceeded on the default (LOW); filed as **BL-17**.
+- **Q:** What are BL-8's 52 variants? The backlog entry records the count, the
+  three failures and the damage classes, not the list; nothing in the tree, the
+  journal or `docs/runs/` holds it. — **risk:** LOW — fixture content; no
+  signature, slice boundary or external format turns on it. — **proposed:**
+  reconstruct 52 from the shipped table's own canonicals across BL-8's damage
+  classes, with the named failures verbatim, and say in the fixture that it is a
+  reconstruction.
+  **Ruling:** proceeded on the default (LOW); endorsed in
+  `docs/oracle/handoff-2026-08-20-2.md`, left for the owner's review. Two facts
+  the owner should see: BL-8's arithmetic (49 matched + 3 failures = 52) does
+  not leave room for the hyphenated `steel-legend` it also reports failing, and
+  the reconstruction has five failing variants, not three.
+- **Q:** Does the table gain `airus master` as well as the observed
+  `airus elite`? R1002 says the table gains "the observed spoken forms", and
+  only the Elite spelling was heard. — **risk:** LOW — one line of data, and
+  deleting the line is the whole reversal. — **proposed:** add it. The
+  mishearing is of `aorus`, the token both family names share, so a table that
+  recovers the Elite and not the Master is inconsistent in a way nothing in the
+  pipeline would ever report.
+  **Ruling:** proceeded on the default (LOW); endorsed in
+  `docs/oracle/handoff-2026-08-20-2.md`, left for the owner's review.
+
+Everything else was **derived**, and the six worth showing rather than asserting:
+
+- **The text the rule runs over.** R1010 settles it: within one cue's normalized
+  text, never across a boundary. This was the HIGH question that stopped the
+  draft; it is answered, so `find_mentions` keeps its one-cue-at-a-time shape
+  and no timestamp question arises — `start_seconds` is always the containing
+  cue's start, which is what R5 cuts windows from and R14 links to.
+- **The required-space reading.** R1002 says "every space inside the alias
+  aligns with a token boundary", which is a *required* boundary, not a tolerated
+  one — otherwise `aorusmaster` would match and the rule would have no floor.
+- **The hyphen-only fold.** R1002 names hyphens and nothing else. Widening to
+  slashes or plus signs would be a fresh reading of R3, which is the design's,
+  not this plan's.
+- **One regex per form, not a token-scanning matcher.** R22 (a channel's worth
+  of captions, one pass) and R23 (byte-identical reruns) both point at the
+  single compiled pattern the built system already has; a rewrite would put both
+  properties back in play for no requirement's benefit.
+- **Where the counter lives.** R1010 asks for a per-run count in the selection
+  report, and R22 forbids holding the corpus in memory — so the count is taken
+  per video, while its transcript is in hand, and summed in
+  `threshold_report`. Persisting it in `selected.jsonl` is then forced rather
+  than chosen: `write_selected`/`read_selected` are contracted to round-trip a
+  `Selection` exactly (`tests/test_select.py`), so a field that did not survive
+  the write would break an existing test.
+- **A stale `selected.jsonl` is an error, not a zero.** R1005 (OD-9) settles the
+  shape: absence and emptiness are different facts and must read differently, and
+  the number the checkpoint is spent against must never quietly understate. A
+  record with no `cross_cue_splits` key is refused, naming the file and the
+  command that rewrites it.
+- **The table's path stays `data/aliases.toml`.** OD-11/R1007 moves it and says
+  the migration is one change of its own — the file and its config default
+  together — so this plan edits the table where it lives and the move carries
+  this content along.
+
+## The work, sliced
+
+Four slices, and they are **sequential**: slice 2's join rule is stated over the
+space slice 1 produces, slice 3's counter is defined in terms of slice 2's
+matcher, and slice 4's variant set is green only once all three have landed.
+They share files for that reason, which is safe because none of them runs
+beside another.
+
+## Slice 1 — A hyphen no longer hides a family name
+
+- **Delivers:** `steel-legend` in a caption or a title matches the table's
+  `Steel Legend`, and `x670e-plus` still matches `X670E`. Observable in
+  `find-best-mobo aliases --check`, where the hyphenated spelling appears in a
+  canonical's `forms:` list instead of being absent. Covers R1002 in part.
+- **Files:** `src/find_best_mobo/normalize.py`, `tests/test_normalize.py`, `tests/test_aliases.py`, `docs/architecture.md`
+- **Estimate:** ~70 lines
+
+### Signatures
+
+```python
+def normalize(text: str) -> str: ...
+```
+
+Unchanged, and deliberately: this is a behaviour change inside a pure function
+every caller already routes through. Nothing else in the module is public, and
+per **OD-12** there is no shared type to place — `src/find_best_mobo/normalize.py`
+defines none and this slice adds none.
+
+### Behaviour the signature cannot carry
+
+- **A hyphen becomes a space** during cleaning, before the joining pass —
+  `normalize("steel-legend") == "steel legend"`, `normalize("The X670E-PLUS
+  board") == "the x670e plus board"`.
+- **The joining rule is unaffected.** `x-670-e` still folds to `x670e`: the
+  hyphen was already a member of `_SEPARATORS`, so a gap that joined before
+  joins now. `_SEPARATORS` collapses to a single space and may be simplified or
+  removed at the coder's discretion, provided the fold cases here hold.
+- **`normalize` stays pure, total and idempotent.** `normalize("")` is `""`, it
+  never raises, and `normalize(normalize(t)) == normalize(t)` — the existing
+  property tests hold unchanged, which is the reason to state it.
+- **The two tests that assert the retired rule are rewritten**, not deleted:
+  `test_hyphen_survives_as_a_character` and
+  `test_hyphenated_model_name_is_left_intact` become the assertions above, and
+  the commit message says why (`AGENTS.md`, the blind-tests rule — editing a
+  test is allowed and must be visible).
+- **`tests/test_aliases.py` is listed only as a contingency.** The hyphen cases
+  there (`the b650e-plus board`, the `X870E-Nova` surface form) normalize on
+  both sides and are expected to pass untouched; if one does not, correcting it
+  belongs to this slice with the reason stated.
+- **`docs/architecture.md`** loses the claim that normalization keeps hyphens —
+  the module's own docstring states it twice and the Components table's
+  normalization row implies it — citing OD-6.
+
+## Slice 2 — A name the captions split in half is still one name
+
+- **Delivers:** `mag tomahawk` matches `the mag toma hawk vrm`, `aorus master`
+  matches `aor us master`, and `b650` still finds nothing in `theb650`. The
+  `aliases --check` report shows the split spelling as the form that fired, and
+  R4's selection counts move for every video whose only mentions were split.
+  Covers R1002.
+- **Files:** `src/find_best_mobo/aliases.py`, `tests/test_aliases.py`, `docs/architecture.md`
+- **Estimate:** ~230 lines
+
+### Signatures
+
+```python
+def alias_pattern(form: str) -> str: ...
+def compile_matcher(aliases: Sequence[Alias]) -> re.Pattern[str]: ...
+```
+
+`alias_pattern` is new and public, in `src/find_best_mobo/aliases.py` alongside
+`compile_matcher`, so the rule has a unit the tests can reach without asserting
+on the shape of the whole table's pattern. `load_aliases`, `find_mentions` and
+`find_title_hits` keep the signatures they have.
+
+Per **OD-12**, the module of every shared type this slice touches, none of which
+changes shape: `Alias` and `Mention` in `src/find_best_mobo/aliases.py`;
+`Transcript` and `Cue` in `src/find_best_mobo/transcripts.py`; `Video` in
+`src/find_best_mobo/index.py`.
+
+### Behaviour the signatures cannot carry
+
+- **`alias_pattern` takes an already-normalized form** and returns regex source
+  for it — no group wrapper and no lookarounds, both of which stay
+  `compile_matcher`'s. Between every pair of adjacent characters inside one word
+  of the form it emits an optional single space; where the form itself has a
+  space it emits a required single space. Every literal character goes through
+  `re.escape`, and no quantifier is nested inside another, so matching stays
+  linear.
+- **`alias_pattern("")` raises `ValueError`.** `compile_matcher` already drops
+  forms that normalize to empty, so it is unreachable from there; an empty
+  pattern would match at every position, which is the failure worth naming.
+- **Tests exercise it by compiling and matching, never by string equality with
+  the regex source.** The source is an implementation detail; the language it
+  accepts is the contract.
+- **What must match**, over normalized text: `toma hawk` → `MAG Tomahawk`;
+  `aor us master` → `Aorus Master`; `tom a hawk` → `MAG Tomahawk` (a split may
+  fall anywhere); `steel leg end` → `Steel Legend` (the alias's space lands on
+  the boundary between `steel` and `leg`); and every form that matched before,
+  unchanged.
+- **What must not match:** `theb650` and `xb650e` (the alias would start inside
+  a token); `b650ex` and `x870ese` (it would end inside one); `aorusmaster` and
+  `steellegend` (the alias's own space has no boundary to land on); `verb 650`
+  (`b650` would start mid-token). These are R1002's "never a proper substring of
+  a fused token", and they are what makes the rule safe rather than merely wide.
+- **Longest-form-first is unchanged**, and still sorts on the length of the
+  *normalized form*, not of its pattern — a stable sort on negated length, file
+  order among equals. `mag tomahawk` therefore still wins over `tomahawk` at the
+  same position, and the compiled pattern stays byte-identical for a given table
+  (R23).
+- **`matched_form` stays `match.group(0)`** — the text as the caption spelled
+  it, so `aliases --check` reports `toma hawk` as the spelling that did the
+  work. That report is R1002's stated measurement; it measures nothing unless
+  the split form survives into it.
+- **Global de-duplication is unchanged.** Two canonicals claiming one normalized
+  form still resolve to the first declared, and the loser still surfaces as a
+  zero-match canonical in the report.
+- **A form's own spaces are single spaces.** Normalized text has no runs and no
+  tabs, so the pattern needs no `+` and gains none — one more thing that cannot
+  drift between two runs.
+- **`docs/architecture.md`**'s "Inspecting the alias table" section gains the
+  join rule beside the longest-first rule, and the alias-table component row
+  says the pattern tolerates caption splits, citing OD-6.
+
+## Slice 3 — The split the rule does not reach is counted, not lost
+
+- **Delivers:** `find-best-mobo select` prints one more line — how many alias
+  matches exist only in the join of two adjacent cues and were therefore *not*
+  emitted as mentions — on every run, zero included. A name broken at a cue
+  break still produces no mention and no excerpt window, and the number saying
+  how often that happened lands in the run records under `docs/runs/` with the
+  rest of the selection report. Covers R1010.
+- **Files:** `src/find_best_mobo/aliases.py`, `src/find_best_mobo/select.py`, `src/find_best_mobo/commands/select.py`, `tests/test_aliases.py`, `tests/test_select.py`, `docs/architecture.md`
+- **Estimate:** ~210 lines
+
+### Signatures
+
+```python
+def count_cross_cue_splits(transcript: Transcript, matcher: re.Pattern[str]) -> int: ...
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class Selection:
+    video: Video
+    reason: str  # "title_hit" | "threshold" | "excluded_below_threshold"
+    mentions: tuple[Mention, ...]
+    distinct_canonicals: int
+    cross_cue_splits: int
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class ThresholdReport:
+    threshold: int
+    title_hits: int
+    threshold_passes: int
+    excluded: int
+    would_include_at_minus_one: int
+    would_exclude_at_plus_one: int
+    cross_cue_splits: int
+```
+
+Per **OD-12**: `count_cross_cue_splits` and `Mention` live in
+`src/find_best_mobo/aliases.py`; `Selection` and `ThresholdReport` in
+`src/find_best_mobo/select.py`, where they are defined today; `Transcript` and
+`Cue` in `src/find_best_mobo/transcripts.py`; `Video` in
+`src/find_best_mobo/index.py`. `select_video`, `select_all`, `threshold_report`,
+`write_selected` and `read_selected` keep the signatures they have — the new
+field travels inside the records they already carry.
+
+### Behaviour the signatures cannot carry
+
+- **The count is over adjacent pairs.** For each pair of consecutive cues
+  `(a, b)`, the joined text is `normalize(a.text + " " + b.text)` — the same
+  single-space join the excerpt cutter uses, so the two stages agree on what
+  "the cues run together" means. The pair contributes
+  `max(0, matches(joined) - matches(normalize(a.text)) - matches(normalize(b.text)))`,
+  and the video's count is the sum over its pairs. A transcript with fewer than
+  two cues counts 0. This is the LOW default filed as **BL-17**; see the
+  Uncertainties.
+- **It never emits a mention, and never changes one.** `find_mentions` is
+  untouched — same shape, same one-cue scan, same `start_seconds`. Nothing
+  downstream of the matcher sees a different mention set because of this slice;
+  the only new output is a number.
+- **It is offline and cheap.** One extra normalize-and-scan per cue boundary,
+  no network and no model spend, exactly as OD-15's rationale assumes. The
+  per-cue match counts may be reused from the work `find_mentions` already did,
+  at the implementer's discretion — the contract is the number, not how often
+  the scan runs.
+- **`select_video` fills the field** for every video, including title hits and
+  exclusions: the count is a property of the transcript, not of the decision
+  taken about it, and a video excluded below the threshold is exactly where a
+  lost mention would matter most.
+- **`threshold_report` sums it** across all selections, excluded ones included.
+  Zero selections is a report with `cross_cue_splits=0`.
+- **The printed line always prints**, including at zero, and says what it means
+  rather than only a number — that these matches were found across a cue
+  boundary and deliberately not counted as mentions, citing R1010. A silent zero
+  and an absent counter must not look alike; that is the whole reason R1010 asks
+  for it.
+- **`selected.jsonl` gains the key `cross_cue_splits`** on each record, written
+  by the same deterministic rules as the rest (sorted keys, compact separators).
+  R23's byte-identical rerun holds: the count is a pure function of the cached
+  transcript and the table.
+- **A record without the key is refused**, not defaulted: `read_selected` raises
+  `ValueError` naming the file and telling the reader to re-run
+  `find-best-mobo select`. This is R1005's rule — absence is an error, and a
+  number the checkpoint is spent against never quietly understates — applied to
+  a stale artifact rather than a missing one. `estimate` surfaces the message
+  rather than crashing on it.
+- **The distinguishing pair R1010 asks for**, in `tests/test_select.py` and
+  `tests/test_aliases.py`: a transcript whose cues break `toma` / `hawk` at the
+  boundary yields **no** mention and a count of 1, and the same text inside one
+  cue yields a mention and a count of 0. Both against the same table, so the
+  only difference is where the cue boundary falls.
+- **`docs/architecture.md`**: the "Narrowing the corpus" path gains the counter
+  as a numbered step, and "Known rough edges" gains the scoping — a name broken
+  at a cue break is not found, on purpose, and the count is how the project will
+  know whether that ever mattered — citing OD-15 and R1010.
+
+## Slice 4 — The measured recall is pinned, and a split-spelled video is selected
+
+- **Delivers:** a fixture of the 52 mangled spellings BL-8 tested, each with the
+  canonical it must reach, run against the shipped table; every one matches, the
+  `air us` mishearings because the table now carries them. And the end of the
+  path OD-6 names as its measurement: a video titled with a split form is
+  selected on its title hit, and one whose only body evidence is split spellings
+  passes the mention threshold instead of being excluded. Covers R1002.
+- **Files:** `tests/fixtures/caption_variants.json`, `tests/test_aliases.py`, `tests/test_select.py`, `data/aliases.toml`, `docs/architecture.md`
+- **Estimate:** ~200 lines
+
+### The fixture
+
+`tests/fixtures/caption_variants.json`, one object:
+
+```json
+{
+  "note": "Reconstructed from BL-8 (OD-6/R1002); see docs/plans/oracle/caption-split-aliases.md",
+  "variants": [{"text": "toma hawk", "canonical": "MAG Tomahawk", "damage": "split"}],
+  "never_match": ["theb650"]
+}
+```
+
+`damage` is one of `spacing`, `digit-split`, `hyphen`, `split`, `spelled-out`,
+`mishearing`, `plural`, `partial` — descriptive, never asserted on, and there so
+a future reader can tell which class a regression belongs to.
+
+**The 52 variants, verbatim.** Each is matched inside a carrier sentence (`the
+<text> board`) as well as bare, so a match at a text boundary and a match
+mid-sentence are both covered. `†` marks the five that fail against the shipped
+table today.
+
